    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS` (the lone `GeneralExceptionHandler - Unexpected error` line is from a test that deliberately triggers an error \u2014 that test passed 5/5).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature following the project's OfficeFloor + generated-DTO conventions. The salutation is derived from a persisted `title` so it survives the round-trip (POST \u2192 GET reloads from the DB).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `title` field to the `OwnerFields` (request) schema and a read-only `salutation` field to the `Owner` (response) schema. DTOs are code-generated from this spec at build time, so `title` and `salutation` now flow through `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` automatically.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `title` column (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, so MapStruct auto-maps the incoming `title` and it's available at read time.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `salutation` mapping backed by a `salutation(owner)` helper: `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just `lastName`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `title` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` test (POST with `title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 GET expects `salutation == \"DR who\"`) passes, along with the entire existing suite. No `@RestController` was introduced \u2014 the existing `BuildOwner` \u2192 mapper pipeline carries the new field.",
